    "notes": "Repo rate is the rate at which the SARB lends to commercial banks. Prime lending rate = Repo + 3.5% (a commercial-bank convention, not set by the SARB). Verified MPC sequence: 2025-07-31 cut to 7.00% (media-reported only; SARB statement not retrieved); 2025-11-20 cut to 6.75% (media-reported); 2026-01-29 hold 6.75%; 2026-03-26 hold 6.75%; 2026-05-28 hike to 7.00% (prime 10.50%, effective 2026-05-29, 4–2); 2026-07-23 hold 7.00% (4–2, two members favoured a hike); 2026-09-23 hike to 7.25% (prime 10.75%, effective 2026-09-25, unanimous). CORRECTION: earlier versions recorded the move to 7.00% as a July 2026 decision dated 2026-07-01; the hike was in May 2026 and July was a hold, held on 2026-07-23. Next MPC: 2026-11-19. Series points before Jul 2025 were not re-verified. The 'automation' block below is from the earlier sarb-adapter run and was not regenerated. SERIES CONVENTION: each point is the repo rate in force after that month's MPC decision. REVIEW: stored 'Jul 2025' (7.25%) and 'Jan 2025' (7.75%) appear to lag one meeting (media report a cut to 7.00% on 2025-07-31; Jan 2025 not checked) — retained unchanged pending verification against SARB MPC statements.",
